<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>\overrightarrow{OA} = \mathbf{a}</m> and <m>\overrightarrow{OB} = \mathbf{b}</m>.</p><p>(a) P divides AB internally in the ratio <m>{2} : {3}</m>. Find <m>\overrightarrow{OP}</m>.</p><div><m>\overrightarrow{OP} =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Q divides AB externally in the ratio <m>{3} : {1}</m>. Find <m>\overrightarrow{OQ}</m>.</p><div><m>\overrightarrow{OQ} =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Internal ratio theorem: <m>\overrightarrow{OP} = \dfrac{n\mathbf{a} + m\mathbf{b}}{m + n} = {\frac{2 \mathbf{b}}{5}+\frac{3 \mathbf{a}}{5}}</m>.</p><p>(b) External ratio theorem: <m>\overrightarrow{OQ} = \dfrac{m\mathbf{b} - n\mathbf{a}}{m - n} = {\frac{3 \mathbf{b}}{2}-\frac{\mathbf{a}}{2}}</m>. The coefficients add to 1 in both.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{2 \mathbf{b}+3 \mathbf{a}}{5}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{3 \mathbf{b}-\mathbf{a}}{2}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>